## The SDLC artifacts

<!-- sdlc-ai:begin artifacts -->
<!-- Managed by sdlc-ai. -->

Work in this repo carries a committed artifact chain in `sdlc/<slug>/`:

| Stage | Artifact | Command |
|---|---|---|
| 1 Plan | `intent.md` — why | `/intent` |
| 2 Design | `spec.md` — what, policy-conformant | `/spec <slug>` |
| 3 Build | `plan.md` — how, reviewed before code | `/plan <slug>` |
| 5 Deploy | review findings | `/review` |
| 6 Maintain | a new `intent.md` | `/close-loop` |

Read `sdlc/README.md` for the rules. Commit each artifact separately from the code — bundling them
destroys both the metric and the evidence that thinking happened first.

